# Drafted by Gemini (R22 n7), edited.

~ throne_start
set n7_started
Narrator: Frost cakes the crooked stone of this ancient cellar, where a blizzard of wailing souls whirls round a throne of black roots. Lord Phillip sits bound in a bramble crown, clutching a lit torch and a winter apple, while Vessla Browntooth hisses nearby in mock angel wings.
phillip_druskenvald [afraid]: Adela was just here, I swear it! She looked right through me, and then the floor gave way and these beastly roots had me by the ankles!
quest crooked_nightmare crooked_throne
-> hub

~ hub
Narrator: The roots creak like ships' timbers in the Perishing cold, holding the King of All fast to his seat.
* [Athletics DC 20] Tear at the roots -> root_ok | root_fail
* [Sleight of Hand DC 20] Work a root loose with fine tools -> root_ok | root_fail
* [Investigation DC 20] Find the knot where the roots join -> root_ok | root_fail
* [if flag.n7_fails >= 3] [Athletics DC 15] The roots have loosened: pull -> root_ok | root_fail
* Help another hero with the roots -> help
* [if not flag.vessla_vision_struck] Strike Vessla -> vessla_hit
* Hear Vessla out -> vessla_talk
* Talk to Phillip -> phillip_talk

~ help
Narrator: {name} braces a boot against the icy stone and hauls back on a thick briar, giving the next pair of hands a fair purchase.
advantage athletics next: help at the roots
-> hub

~ root_ok
Narrator: With a sharp crack of frost, one of the great roots splinters and uncoils from Phillip's chest.
set n7_roots += 1
-> tick

~ root_fail
Narrator: The bramble crown twists of its own accord and the torch in Phillip's stiff hand flares out, scorching {name}'s knuckles.
damage 4d6 fire
set n7_fails += 1
-> tick

~ vessla_hit
nm_vessla [angry]: Touch not the messenger, little mice, or keep the fire and choke on the smoke!
Narrator: Your blow passes through weasel fur and tarnished tinsel; she dissolves with a wet hiss, leaving her burning gold blade ringing upon the ice.
vanish nm_vessla
set vessla_vision_struck
give flame_tongue
-> hub

~ vessla_talk
nm_vessla [sly]: Stonoga salts the meat and Golub plucks the thoughts, clumsy sisters both. Only I know how to pare a soul down to the wick, crowning her sweet lord so her heart breaks clean for the pot.
-> hub

~ phillip_talk
phillip_druskenvald [weary]: King of All, they call me! Quite the coronation, wouldn't you say, though the crown is dreadfully tight and I daren't drop this apple.
phillip_druskenvald [afraid]: Never mind my fingers, have you seen Adela? She was terribly pale, and the attic stairs were bleeding pitch.
-> hub

~ tick
Narrator: A bitter gust sweeps off the Frozen Throne, riming your eyelashes and stealing the breath from your lungs.
check Constitution DC 15 -> tick_soul | tick_cold

~ tick_cold
Narrator: The cellar cold bites deep into the marrow, numbing fingers and joints alike.
damage 2d6 cold
-> tick_soul

~ tick_soul
Narrator: Pale faces spin out of the driving snow, their open mouths keening at the edges of your mind.
check Charisma DC 15 -> tick_end | tick_souls

~ tick_souls
Narrator: Dead fingers rake through your thoughts, leaving a trail of grief that is not your own.
damage 1d6 psychic
-> tick_end

~ tick_end
if flag.n7_roots >= 6
-> freed
else
-> hub
endif

~ freed
Narrator: The last root snaps like an icicle, and Phillip pitches forward into a rising coil of Dani's blue porch-mist.
phillip_druskenvald [afraid]: Adela! Hold on, my darling, I'm coming, I'm right behind them!
Narrator: He is already running when the mist takes him whole, and in the tangled roots behind the empty throne, a crooked door begins to glow red.
cutscene nm_pulled_out
Narrator: A hand of blue mist closes round a hand, and the captive is drawn up and out of the dream.
cutscene nm_pulled_out_2
Narrator: Far away on the porch, Dani keeps her eyes shut, and a thread of blue light runs from her hands into the house.
cutscene end
vanish phillip_druskenvald
set phillip_freed
set nm_throne_done
if not flag.vessla_vision_struck
Narrator: Vessla's painted halo gutters out like a tallow dip, and her flaming sword clatters onto the frost.
give flame_tongue
endif
quest crooked_nightmare toil_and_trouble
-> END

~ door
if not flag.nm_throne_done
Narrator: Black roots knot the reddish frame shut, pulsing slow and cold in time with the throne.
-> END
else
Narrator: The reddish door sits crookedly among the severed roots, smelling faintly of cauldron steam and singed hair.
* Step through the roots -> pass
* [Performance DC 12] Tell the roots a joke -> joke_ok | joke_fail
* Not yet -> END
endif

~ joke_ok
Narrator: A dry snicker runs through the knotted wood, and the frost along the lintel thaws by a hand's width.
set dream_laughed
-> pass

~ joke_fail
Narrator: The roots keep their counsel, stiff and winter-mean as ever.
-> pass

~ pass
Narrator: The roots part without asking a toll, letting you up toward the heat of the attic.
quest crooked_nightmare toil_and_trouble
move nm_attic
-> END
